there is a deficiency.\nAnswer___________", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 1128, "answer": {"text": "C", "source": {"id": "offline-7060983eb3e76b90744a", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 17.pdf", "sha256": "7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 3, "prompt": "Higher and lower level of the metabolic hormones.\nAnswer ____________", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 1196, "answer": {"text": "D", "source": {"id": "offline-7060983eb3e76b90744a", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 17.pdf", "sha256": "7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 4, "prompt": "Known to affect the interior surface of blood vessels and lymphatic vessels.\nAnswer ____________", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 1271, "answer": {"text": "A", "source": {"id": "offline-7060983eb3e76b90744a", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 17.pdf", "sha256": "7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 5, "prompt": "Worsening relative sugar equilibrium.\nAnswer _____________", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 1373, "answer": {"text": "B", "source": {"id": "offline-7060983eb3e76b90744a", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 17.pdf", "sha256": "7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 8, "prompt": "What defines the rate of myocardial relaxation?\nAnswer___________", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 369, "answer": {"text": "Lusitropy", "source": {"id": "offline-7060983eb3e76b90744a", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 17.pdf", "sha256": "7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 9, "prompt": "What are more associated with insulin resistance?\nAnswer ___________", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 440, "answer": {"text": "Low serum Gal-3 concentrations", "source": {"id": "offline-7060983eb3e76b90744a", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 17.pdf", "sha256": "7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 10, "prompt": "What can have the potential to have direct impact on insulin resistance?\nAnswer ____________", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 514, "answer": {"text": "Gal-3", "source": {"id": "offline-7060983eb3e76b90744a", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 17.pdf", "sha256": "7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 11, "prompt": "What defines an abnormal amount of lipids?\nAnswer _____________", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 613, "answer": {"text": "Dyslipidemia", "source": {"id": "offline-7060983eb3e76b90744a", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 17.pdf", "sha256": "7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 12, "prompt": "What are the markers of biomechanical cardiac stress?\nAnswer______________", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 683, "answer": {"text": "NP levels", "source": {"id": "offline-7060983eb3e76b90744a", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 17.pdf", "sha256": "7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 13, "prompt": ".What is associated with programmed cell death?\nAnswer___________", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 764, "answer": {"text": "Gal- 3", "source": {"id": "offline-7060983eb3e76b90744a", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 17.pdf", "sha256": "7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 14, "prompt": "What causes the cardiac wall to stretch and volume overload of cardiac\ncavities?\nAnswer____________", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 835, "answer": {"text": "NP secretion", "source": {"id": "offline-7060983eb3e76b90744a", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 17.pdf", "sha256": "7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}], "skills": ["reading"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-7060983eb3e76b90744a", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 17.pdf", "sha256": "7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}], "passages": []}, {"id": "af71f2fed55b0c72-p5", "label": "Part B · Questions 15-20", "part": "B", "sourceSha256": "af71f2fed55b0c72520a74cf78776e256bfbdf3c800973be8f6c69deecb75faa", "pages": [5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11], "questions": [{"number": 15, "prompt": "_______________ can be associated with a significantly increased risk for\ncoronary heart disease.", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 156}, {"number": 16, "prompt": ".higher levels of brain NP can be connected with the decreased risk\nof___________", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 259}, {"number": 17, "prompt": ".The term_____________ is referred to the thickening and scarring of\nconnective tissue, usually as a result of an injury.", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 345}, {"number": 18, "prompt": "It is still not clear that Gal-3 is a ______________ of the metabolically\nunh.ealthy obese", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 471}, {"number": 19, "prompt": "Excretion of sodium in the urine is a common condition and is\ncalled ______________", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 567}, {"number": 20, "prompt": "NPs may not mediate __________ of lipids.\nPART B\nIn this part of the test, there are six short extracts relating to the work of health\nprofessionals. For questions 1-6, choose the answer (A, B or C) which you think\nfits best according to the text.", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 656}, {"number": 1, "prompt": "What is correct about liver toxicity from sulfasalazine?\nHepatotoxicity can arise either from direct toxicity of the drug or its\nmetabolites.\nIn rare cases, it can be immune mediated.\nImmune-mediated toxicity is believed to be due to an idiosyncratic delayed-\ntype hypersensitivity reaction.", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 948, "answer": {"text": "Hepatotoxicity can arise either from direct toxicity of the drug or its metabolites.", "source": {"id": "offline-7060983eb3e76b90744a", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 17.pdf", "sha256": "7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 5, "prompt": "What is correct about the survey?\nMales were accounted for 53% of total participants\n43% participants had a bachelor degree of pharmacy\n71% were practicing as pharmacists\nTwo hundred and six of the 250 pharmacists completed the questionnaires, giving a response rate of\n82.4%. The mean age of pharmacists was approximately 32 years with a majority in the young adult\nage group (20-50 years, 92.22%).\nSociodemographic parameter                             Respondents, N=206(%)\nAge (yr) Mean (SD)                                     36\nGender\n128\nMale\n78\nFemale\nEducation qualification\n164\nGraduate(B. Pharm, D. Pharm)\n42\nPostgraduate(M. Pharm)", "sourcePage": 9, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 0, "answer": {"text": "71% were practicing as pharmacists", "source": {"id": "offline-7060983eb3e76b90744a", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 17.pdf", "sha256": "7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}], "skills": ["reading"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-7060983eb3e76b90744a", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 17.pdf", "sha256": "7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}], "passages": []}, {"id": "af71f2fed55b0c72-p12", "label": "Part C · PART C", "part": "C", "sourceSha256": "af71f2fed55b0c72520a74cf78776e256bfbdf3c800973be8f6c69deecb75faa", "pages": [12, 13, 14, 15, 16, 17, 18, 19, 20], "questions": [{"number": 15, "prompt": "to 23 percent of new asthma cases in adults are work related. Four states\n(California, New Jersey, Massachusetts, and Michigan) tracked cases of", "sourcePage": 12, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1724, "answer": {"text": "Inflammation", "source": {"id": "offline-7060983eb3e76b90744a", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 17.pdf", "sha256": "7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 9, "prompt": "According to paragraph 2, OLDs are;\nIncurable\nCurable\nPreventable but not curable\nCurable and preventable", "sourcePage": 14, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 500, "answer": {"text": "Preventable but not curable", "source": {"id": "offline-7060983eb3e76b90744a", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 17.pdf", "sha256": "7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 10, "prompt": "According to paragraph 2, 'work-related asthma' means;\nA disease which occurs due to more work\nA disease which occurs due to less work\nA disease which occurs due to exposure to work", "sourcePage": 14, "choices": ["A"], "kind": "question", "offset": 629, "answer": {"text": "None of the above", "source": {"id": "offline-7060983eb3e76b90744a", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 17.pdf", "sha256": "7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 22, "prompt": "What happens if the responses become exaggerated?\nLoss of memory may take place.\nReduction in normal mood may be noted.\nCognitive impairment occurs.\nAcute pain may begin.", "sourcePage": 20, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 0, "answer": {"text": "Cognitive impairment occurs.", "source": {"id": "offline-7060983eb3e76b90744a", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 17.pdf", "sha256": "7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/7060983eb3e76b90744a31d3239effc358c625260b4728be8d982693199b2ec0.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}], "skills": ["reading"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline